title: Eisner is murdered!
subtitle: 21 February. The Bavarian premier is shot in a Munich street.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1919 and month = 2 and crisis = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 1
on-arrival: {!
RG.news('Kurt Eisner shot dead in Munich', 3);
RG.district('bavaria', {militancy: 10});
!}

= Eisner is murdered!

Kurt Eisner, the Independent premier of Bavaria, was walking to the Landtag with his resignation in his pocket when Count Anton von Arco auf Valley shot him in the back. Within hours a council member shot the Social Democratic leader Erhard Auer in the chamber. The Landtag has fled. A Central Council rules Munich, and the barracks fly red flags.

Our Munich group is small and divided. The Zentrale must decide what it wants from Bavaria.

- @levine: Send Eugen Leviné to take the Munich party in hand.
- @republic: Call for a Bavarian council republic now.
- @congress: Back the Congress of Councils and the Independents.

@levine
subtitle: A disciplined party first. Munich's Communists will be ready, and they will be few.
on-arrival: levine_sent = 1; bav_prep = 1; lean_luxemburgist += 2; district_bavaria_loyalty += 10

Leviné, a veteran of 1905 who ran our paper in the Ruhr, takes the night train to Munich. Within weeks the Munich party has membership cards, a printing press and a line.

@republic
subtitle: The barracks will listen. So will the priests, and they will tell the peasants.
on-arrival: bav_prep = 2; lean_offensive += 2; district_bavaria_members += 0.4

Our speakers call for a Bavarian Soviet Republic at every meeting. The soldiers applaud.

@congress
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Independents run the food offices. They will remember who stood with them.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any alliance with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.bav_prep = 3;
Q.uspd_relation += 6;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

In March the Landtag returns and elects the Social Democrat Johannes Hoffmann premier. The councils remain, for now.
